        High-order Lagrangian Hydrodynamics Miniapp


Version 3.2
=============================

- Added CMake build support for CPU, CUDA and HIP configurations, with optional
  RAJA support, and separate CMake and Makefile installation instructions.

- Updated compatibility MFEM 4.10. CMake builds use C++17 by default and C++20
  when MFEM enables RAJA or Umpire.

- Added optional user.cmake and user.mk files for local build configuration, and
  improved Makefile support for externally built or installed MFEM libraries.

- Added configurable Cartesian mesh resolutions (-nx, -ny, -nz) and domain
  sizes (-Sx, -Sy, -Sz).

- Replaced the Cartesian partitioning options (-c and -pt) with mesh generation
  based on the number of elements per MPI task (-epm). Nonzero -epm is mutually
  exclusive with explicit mesh resolution and refinement options. METIS is
  optional when using generated meshes.

- Added support for selecting non-conforming meshes (-nc, enabled by default
  in 2D and 3D) or conforming meshes (-no-nc).

- Added an analytical Sedov blast solution in sedov/, a standalone sedov
  executable, and comparison of the simulated density against the exact
  solution (-err).

- Added configurable Sedov blast energy (-E0, default 1) and delta-function
  projection tolerance (-dtol). Scale the deposited energy by 1/2^dim to account
  for the simulated portion of the symmetric blast, and detect non-finite
  initial conditions.

- Added optional Caliper profiling annotations and Adiak metadata for run
  configuration, timings, figures of merit and device memory usage.

- Added a shared Umpire device memory pool for hypre and MFEM, with configurable
  initial size (-pool), pool warm-up and high-water mark diagnostics.

- Added partial assembly kernels for linear kinematic and constant energy
  spaces (-ok 1 -ot 0) in 2D and 3D, and fifth-order kinematic and fourth-order
  energy spaces (-ok 5 -ot 4) in 2D. Added missing MFEM quadrature interpolation
  and mass integrator specializations.

- Fixed internal and kinetic energy evaluation on simplex meshes and MPI ranks
  with empty local meshes, and geometric factor handling for 2D Taylor-Green.

- Fixed GPU benchmark timing by synchronizing device computations, integer
  overflow in global mesh sizes and timing counters, and reporting of GPU-aware
  MPI configuration.

- Updated regression tests and checks for mesh generation and Sedov energy
  changes, made test result extraction more robust, and updated GitHub CI to use
  shared MFEM actions.


Version 3.1, released on Apr 9, 2021
====================================

- New version compatible with MFEM v4.2.

- Added new examples: Taylor-Green instability and 3D Triple Point.

- Support for device computations of internal and kinetic energy.


Version 3.0, released on Mar 27, 2020
=====================================

- Replaced the Laghos-2.0 custom implementations in the cuda/, raja/, occa/ and
  hip/ directories with direct general device support in the main Laghos sources
  based on MFEM-4.1

- With the above change different device backends can be selected at runtime,
  including cuda, raja, occa, hip, omp and more. See the -d command-line option.

- Added 'setup' makefile target to download and build the Laghos dependencies:
  HYPRE (2.11.2), METIS (4.0.3) and MFEM (master branch).

- Added 'tests' and 'checks' makefile targets to launch non-regression tests.

- Added default dimension options that generate internally the mesh:
  * 1D (-dim 1): data/segment01.mesh
  * 2D (-dim 2): data/square01_quad.mesh
  * 3D (-dim 3): data/cube01_hex.mesh

- The timing/ directory was deprecated. Use the scripts in the CEED benchmarks
  instead, https://github.com/CEED/benchmarks.


Version 2.0, released on Nov 19, 2018
=====================================

- Added a CUDA version of Laghos in the cuda/ directory.

- Added a RAJA version of Laghos in the raja/ directory.

- Added an OCCA version of Laghos in the occa/ directory.

- Added an AMR (adaptive mesh refinement) version in the amr/ directory.

- Replaced a viscosity "if statement" with a smooth step function.

- When using partial assembly (-pa option), support the Bernstein positive basis
  for the velocity .

- Added Travis CI regression testing on GitHub.


Version 1.1, released on Sep 28, 2018
=====================================

- Added a new example: Gresho vortex.

- Added instructions for building the CUDA and RAJA versions.

- Added a conservative time integrator (RK2Avg).

- Added computation of total energy.

- Split the LagrangianHydroOperator::Mult() into separate functions for
  assembly, velocity solve, internal energy solve.

- Improved the computations of the matrix diagonal by contracting the squares of
  the B matrices.

- Added diagonal preconditioners for both partial and full assembly.

- Fixed a bug in the evaluation of the material gamma values.

- Additional meshes that can be used for scaling tests.


Version 1.0, released on Dec 7, 2017
====================================

- Initial release.
